{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And he begot a son.</b> And it does not write 'and he begot Noah,' as with the others — a hint that from him the world would be built, for the entire world was destroyed in the days of the Flood, and he and his sons remained. Another explanation: Methuselah the righteous gave him advice not to hurry to give him a name, because the men of that generation were sorcerers, and they would cast a spell upon him if they knew his name."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:02.213714721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}